Subject: [PATCH 305/305] CLAUDE.md -- 0300-0303 flashed, 0304, and the
 first-join timing

The board result for the 0300 series, which is that there is no board
result. v0.3.0-138-gc2dd970 boots clean and identical in shape to the run
before it, the RADIO tab was tapped, and it said `radio: 0 stations` --
so not one line of 0300-0303 has drawn a pixel. Worth recording as its
own kind of outcome rather than as progress: two flashes have confirmed
the patches compile and confirmed nothing else. The 0200 series' lesson
was flash early, and this is the other half of it -- flashing early does
nothing if the path cannot be reached.

So the entry names the two steps that would reach it, in order, and says
plainly that the second has never been run: write a stations.m3u and
press RLOD, then play a tagged file BEFORE picking a station, which is
the order 0300 exists for and the order no run has used.

Two open items closed by 0304, one of them in the 0200 list, with the
reason the obstacle was real kept rather than deleted.

And the first-join failure, which is not this series and is in both logs.
wifi_join()'s comment block already has the 6.6 s and the six flashes
behind the whole-attempt retry; what is new is that it is reproducible to
about twenty milliseconds across runs, and that in both of these the
failing attempt was issued within 13 ms of a 30-network scan finishing.
Recorded as a hypothesis with the counter-evidence beside it -- the sixth
flash had a reason 2 with no scan before it -- and explicitly not
patched. The cyan flash cost six patches for chasing a mechanism before
measuring it.
